  "unit": "u07-directions",
  "title": "Rickshaw & CNG",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "Hailing a rickshaw in Bangladesh goes like this: call **এই রিকশা!**, then name your destination and ask **যাবেন?** 'Will you go?' Drivers are addressed as **মামা** or **ভাই**.\n\n**যাব** = 'I/we will go', **যাবেন** = 'you (polite) will go'. Destinations often need no ending at all in speech: **ধানমন্ডি যাবেন?** 'Will you go to Dhanmondi?'\n\nAgree the fare *before* you get in: **ভাড়া কত?** If it's high, use your Unit 6 haggling: **ভাড়া একটু বেশি**.\n\nTo get off: **মামা, এখানে থামেন** 'Stop here, please'. A **সিএনজি** is the green gas-powered auto-rickshaw — in Kolkata it's an **অটো**.",
